    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0373" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/2807: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Casablanca</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Casablanca</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-03T16:00:00+01:00">June 3, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>228. Reference Consulate’s 209, May 25, 7 p.m. Rouvier, acting for Monick now at
                    Vichy, stated yesterday that it was imperative that French Protectorate
                    authorities be informed as soon as possible whether economic accord is going
                    into effect. He further stated that an answer in the negative was better than
                    none at all. Furthermore he stated that it was advisable that I should be able
                    to inform Monick when I made my introductory official calls at Rabat, which
                    should be made this week. I regret to appear to be in the position of seeming to
                    force the Department’s hand but the above absolutely represents the statements
                    made today. Rouvier also said that the Vichy Government had telegraphed to Rabat
                    that it had requested our Government to obtain from the British release of
                    French vessels <hi rendition="#italic">Schéhérazade</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winnipeg</hi> and to put accord into effect. The above
                    statements were made in the presence of Stanton<anchor n="92" xml:id="d302-f1"/>
                    and the individual<anchor n="93" xml:id="d302-f2"/> mentioned in Department’s 21
                    of January 29<anchor n="94" xml:id="d302-f3"/> as well as myself.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tangier and Vichy with request to the latter to inform Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
